cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SIS3316 DAQ & Analysis Software"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Karakas"
    given-names: "Yavuz Selim"
    email: "selim.karakas@tu-dortmund.de"
    affiliation: "Technische Universität Dortmund"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1349-3149"
abstract: >-
  A C++17 / Qt6 / CERN ROOT acquisition and analysis suite for the Struck
  SIS3316-250-14 (16-channel, 250 MS/s, 14-bit) digitizer. Provides live Ethernet acquisition,
  full in-GUI hardware configuration, FPGA lookup-table coincidence triggering
  (AND / OR / multiplicity), direct-to-ROOT recording, and native offline
  analysis including charge-comparison pulse-shape discrimination, Figure-of-
  Merit, spectra with bounded Gaussian fitting, and multi-detector coincidence
  (time-of-flight, coincidence matrix, accidental estimation).
keywords:
  - SIS3316
  - data acquisition
  - pulse-shape discrimination
  - organic scintillator
  - neutron-gamma discrimination
  - coincidence trigger
  - CERN ROOT
  - Qt
license: MIT
